; `:walk-opaque true` stops every descent, not just the validator's.
;
; `(phrase :name origin)` is written by the author, inside the opaque
; `:body` slot. The cross-ref index pass does not descend there any more,
; so `origin` is never registered and the `:anchor origin` below finds an
; empty registry.
;
; This is the half that changes what an authored document *means*, and it
; is the point of the flag: a subtree the surrounding schema declined to
; interpret is not a place to harvest cross-ref targets, lexical scopes or
; cycle edges out of. The validator will not tell you anything about
; what is in there; neither will it quietly use it.
;
; Move the same `(phrase …)` one key over into a slot the schema reads and
; it registers as it always did.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name phrase-name
    :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target phrase))
  (form :name phrase
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))
  (form :name host
    (key :name body :type any :walk-opaque true :optional true))
  (form :name track
    (key :name anchor :type phrase-name :optional true)))

(host :body (phrase :name origin))
(track :anchor origin)
